\f8\b\fs28 \cf2 3. PHASE 17R SUMMARY\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs18 \cf2 Phase 17R was opened after Mini Jarvis encountered a logging-related I/O error during extended use. The error appeared after the system had been idle or in Deep mode for several hours. The observed failure was related to saving the conversation log, not to the model response itself.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf2 Observed error:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs18 \cf2 [Errno 5] Input/output error: '/home/minijarvis/logs/conversations'\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf2 Important distinction:\
The model response should never be lost, interrupted, or blocked merely because the conversation log cannot be written. Phase 17R therefore changed logging from a required-success operation into a best-effort operation.\
\
Result:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs18 \cf2 Phase 17R completed successfully. Fast mode and Deep mode were both tested afterward and passed.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f8\b\fs28 \cf2 4. REQUIRED NON-FATAL LOGGING PROTECTION\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs22 \cf2 The canonical source file remains:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs18 \cf2 /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/jarvis_ui.py\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf2 The logging call in jarvis_ui.py must remain protected so that a logging exception cannot break the GUI response flow. The required pattern is:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs18 \cf2 model_label = next((label for label, exact_name in MODEL_OPTIONS.items() if exact_name == model_name), model_name)\
conversation_history += f"\\nUser: \{prompt\}\\nAssistant: \{response_text\}"\
\
try:\
    append_conversation_log(prompt, response_text, model_label, model_name)\
except Exception as e:\
    root.after(0, update_text, f"\\n[Warning: conversation log was not saved: \{e\}]\\n")\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf2 Do not revert this to an unprotected append_conversation_log call. The protected try and except block is now part of the official stable operating baseline.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f8\b\fs28 \cf2 5. UPDATED CONVERSATION LOGGING POLICY\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs22 \cf2 Conversation logging remains enabled and should continue to use one daily file with a 60-day retention period. Model metadata should remain included for each exchange.\
\
Updated policy:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Conversation logging is best-effort.\
\'95	A successful model response must still display in the GUI even if log writing fails.\
\'95	A logging error may show a warning in the GUI, but it must not terminate the response flow.\
\'95	The conversation_history variable should still be updated even if file logging fails.\
\'95	The log directory remains /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/logs/conversations/.\
\'95	The file pattern remains conversation_YYYY-MM-DD.txt.\
\'95	The retention policy remains 60 days.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f8\b\fs28 \cf2 6. UPDATED KNOWN LIMITATION: IDLE I/O AND DESKTOP INPUT ISSUE\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs22 \cf2 Add the following known limitation to the canonical documentation.\
\
After approximately 5 hours in Deep mode or extended idle/deep-model use, Mini Jarvis showed a logging I/O error and the Raspberry Pi desktop lost mouse movement. Keyboard input into the GUI text box still appeared, but mouse movement failed. SSH connections also reset or closed during the same event. A power reboot restored normal operation.\
\
Current status:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Recovered after reboot.\
\'95	Mouse movement restored after reboot.\
\'95	Mini Jarvis booted normally after reboot.\
\'95	Fast mode passed after reboot.\
\'95	Deep mode passed after reboot.\
\'95	Phase 17R made conversation logging failure non-fatal.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Possible future diagnostic areas:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Storage I/O or external SSD behavior.\
\'95	Desktop input stack or GUI session stability.\
\'95	SSH service stability.\
\'95	Thermal behavior under longer Deep model use.\
\'95	Power stability under sustained load.\
\'95	Long-idle behavior while Qwen3 remains resident.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 This issue is not considered a blocker after Phase 17R, but it should remain documented because the root cause was not fully isolated.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

